# OpenSignature

The product / project name is **OpenSignature**.

- Use `OpenSignature` in user-facing text, README, docs titles, UI branding, and commit/PR titles when referring to the product.
- Technical assembly/namespace prefixes are `OpenSignature.*` (projects under `src/` and `tests/`).
- Do not invent alternate product names (e.g. "E-Signature Platform" alone without OpenSignature) in new UI or docs.

Follow `.cursor/skills/esign-platform-development/SKILL.md`.
Follow `.cursor/skills/commit-after-task/SKILL.md` after every completed task.

Use `docs/PRODUCT-SPEC.en.md` and `docs/TASKS.md` as the primary engineering sources of truth.

Implement work task-by-task. Update task status only when tests and acceptance criteria pass.

All code, identifiers, comments, logs, tests and commit messages must be English.

Never commit secrets, private keys, PFX files or credentials.

Do not put document binaries in RabbitMQ messages.

Do not expose or export private keys from HSM/smart-card/PKCS#11 providers.

After every completed task, create a Conventional Commit with a meaningful English message. Do not leave completed work uncommitted.
